4.2 Groups and rows
===================

     (keymap-popup-define my-feed-map
       :group "Navigation"
       "n" ("Next" next-line :stay-open t)
       "p" ("Previous" previous-line :stay-open t)
       :group "Tags"
       "r" ("Toggle read" my-feed-toggle-read :stay-open t)
       :row
       :group "Feeds"
       "A" ("Add feed" my-feed-add)
       "D" ("Remove feed" my-feed-remove))

   At display time, groups flow from left to right and automatically
continue on another display row when the popup window is too narrow.
This applies even when the declaration contains no ‘:row’.  An
individual group wider than the window is truncated with an ellipsis
rather than disturbing the column alignment.

   ‘:row’ between groups forces a fresh row beneath the first regardless
of the available width.  Groups may attach their own predicates: ‘:group
("Bulk" :if PRED :inapt-if PRED)’.


